ll,"title":null,"property":"P1365","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Northern Rhodesia"},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flag of Zambia.svg","from_t":1996,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"coat","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Coat of arms of Zambia.svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P94","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q105480","value_label":"Kenneth Kaunda","from_t":1964.811475409836,"to_t":1991.835616438356,"title":"President of Zambia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Kenneth Kaunda"},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q153986","value_label":"Guy Scott","from_t":2014.8219178082193,"to_t":2015.0657534246575,"title":"President of Zambia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Guy Scott"},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q18352991","value_label":"Edgar Lungu","from_t":2015.0657534246575,"to_t":2021.6438356164383,"title":"President of Zambia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Edgar Lungu"},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q212058","value_label":"Levy Mwanawasa","from_t":2002.0027397260274,"to_t":2008.6311475409836,"title":"President of Zambia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Levy Mwanawasa"},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q217500","value_label":"Rupiah Banda","from_t":2008.6010928961748,"to_t":2011.7260273972602,"title":"President of Zambia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Rupiah Banda"},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q297057","value_label":"Frederick Chiluba","from_t":1991.835616438356,"to_t":2002.0027397260274,"title":"President of Zambia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Frederick Chiluba"},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q299173","value_label":"Michael Sata","from_t":2011.7260273972602,"to_t":2014.8219178082193,"title":"President of Zambia","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Michael Sata"},{"qid":"Q953","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q170814","value_label":"Flag of Zambia.svg","from_t":1964.811475409836,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Zambia","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Zambia"}],"people":{"Q717185":{"label":"Hakainde Hichilema","description":"President of Zambia since 2021","enwiki":"Hakainde Hichilema","summary":"Hakainde Hichilema (born 4 June 1962), often known by his initials HH and the nickname \"Bally\", is a Zambian businessman, farmer, and politician who is the seventh and current president of Zambia since 24 August 2021. Since the death of Guy Scott in 2026, he is the only living person who has been president of Zambia.\nHichilema has led the United Party for National Development since 2006, following the death of party founder Anderson Mazoka. Prior to his election, he was a major opponent of Edgar Lungu, who was president from 2015 to 2021.","image":"Hakainde Hichilema in Japan on February 6, 2025 (cropped).jpg","birth":1962.4219178082192,"death":null},"Q18352991":{"label":"Edgar Lungu","description":"President of Zambia from 2015 to 2021 (1956–2025)","enwiki":"Edgar Lungu","summary":"Edgar Chagwa Lungu (11 November 1956 – 5 June 2025) was a Zambian politician who served as the sixth president of Zambia from 26 January 2015 to 24 August 2021.\nUnder President Michael Sata, Lungu served as Minister of Justice and Minister of Defence. Following Sata's death in October 2014, Lungu was nominated as the candidate for the Patriotic Front at the Convention of the Patriotic Front which was held in Kabwe, for the January 2015 presidential by-election, which was to determine who would serve out the remainder of Sata's term. In the election, he narrowly defeated opposition candidate Hakainde Hichilema and took office on 25 January 2015.","image":"Edgar Lungu in TICAD VII (cropped).jpg","birth":1956.860655737705,"death":2025.4246575342465},"Q105480":{"label":"Kenneth Kaunda","description":"First president of Zambia (1924–2021)","enwiki":"Kenneth Kaunda","summary":"Kenneth Kaunda (28 April 1924 – 17 June 2021), also known as KK, was a Zambian politician who served as the first president of Zambia from 1964 to 1991. He was at the forefront of the campaign for independence from the British Empire, though he would subsequently establish himself as a dictator and oversee Zambia's economic collapse once this was achieved. Dissatisfied with Harry Nkumbula's leadership of the Northern Rhodesian African National Congress, he broke away and founded the Zambian African National Congress, later becoming the head of the socialist United National Independence Party (UNIP).\nKaunda was the first president of independent Zambia.","image":"Kenneth David Kaunda.jpg","birth":1924.3224043715848,"death":2021.4575342465753},"Q153986":{"label":"Guy Scott","description":"Zambian politician (1944-2026)","enwiki":"Guy Scott","summary":"Guy Lindsay Scott (1 June 1944 – 15 July 2026) was a Zambian politician who served as acting president of Zambia from 2014 to 2015 and was the 12th vice president from 2011 to 2014. Scott became acting president upon Michael Sata's death in office on 28 October 2014. This made him the first head of state of European descent in mainland Africa since F. W. de Klerk in 1994.","image":"Guy Scott.png","birth":1944.4153005464482,"death":2026.5342465753424},"Q212058":{"label":"Levy Mwanawasa","description":"former President of Zambia (1948-2008)","enwiki":"Levy Mwanawasa","summary":"Levy Patrick Mwanawasa (3 September 1948 – 19 August 2008) was a Zambian politician who served as the third president of Zambia. He served as president from January 2002 until his death in August 2008. Mwanawasa is credited with having initiated a campaign to rid the corruption situation in Zambia during his term. Prior to Mwanawasa's election, he served as the fourth vice-president of Zambia from November 1991 to July 1994, whilst an elected Member of Parliament of Chifubu Constituency.","image":"Levy Mwanawasa.jpg","birth":1948.672131147541,"death":2008.6311475409836},"Q217500":{"label":"Rupiah Banda","description":"4th president of Zambia (2008–2011); 1937–2022","enwiki":"Rupiah Banda","summary":"Rupiah Bwezani Banda (19 February 1937 – 11 March 2022) was a Zambian politician who served as the fourth president of Zambia from 2008 to 2011, taking over from Levy Mwanawasa. Banda was an active participant in politics from early in the presidency of Kenneth Kaunda, during which time he held several diplomatic posts.\nIn October 2006, he was appointed the vice-president by Mwanawasa. After Mwanawasa suffered a stroke in June 2008 and died later that year, he became acting president.","image":"Rupiah Banda.jpg","birth":1937.1178082191782,"death":2022.1890410958904},"Q297057":{"label":"Frederick Chiluba","description":"former President of Zambia (1991–2002)","enwiki":"Frederick Chiluba","summary":"Frederick Jacob Titus Chiluba (30 April 1943 – 18 June 2011) was a Zambian politician who was the second president of Zambia from 1991 to 2002. Chiluba, a trade union leader, won the country's multi-party presidential election in 1991 as the candidate of the Movement for Multi-party Democracy (MMD), defeating long-time President Kenneth Kaunda. He was re-elected in 1996. As he was unable to run for a third term in 2001, former Vice President Levy Mwanawasa instead ran as the MMD candidate and succeeded him.","image":"Frederick Chiluba on February 3, 1994 (cropped).jpg","birth":1943.3260273972603,"death":2011.4602739726026},"Q299173":{"label":"Michael Sata","description":"Zambian politician (1937–2014)","enwiki":"Michael Sata","summary":"Michael Charles Chilufya Sata (6 July 1937 – 28 October 2014) was a Zambian politician who served as the fifth president of Zambia from 2011 until his death in 2014. A social democrat, he led the Patriotic Front (PF), a major political party in Zambia. Under President Frederick Chiluba, Sata was a minister during the 1990s as part of the Movement for Multiparty Democracy (MMD) government. He went into opposition in 2001, forming the PF.\nAs an opposition leader, Sata – popularly known as \"The King Cobra\", emerged as the leading opposition presidential contender and rival to President Levy Mwanawasa in the 2006 presidential election, but was defeated.","image":"Michael Chilufya Sata on April 2, 2014 (cropped).jpg","birth":1937.509589041096,"death":2014.8219178082193}},"media":{"Flag of Zambia.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Flag_of_Zambia.svg/330px-Flag_of_Zambia.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Zambia.svg","author":"Gabriel Ellison","license":"Public domain"},"Coat of arms of Zambia.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Coat_of_arms_of_Zambia.svg/330px-Coat_of_arms_of_Zambia.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Zambia.svg","author":"FXXX","license":"Public domain"},"Hakainde Hichilema in Japan on February 6, 2025 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Hakainde_Hichilema_in_Japan_on_February_6%2C_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Hakainde_Hichilema_in_Japan_on_February_6%2C_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hakainde_Hichilema_in_Japan_on_February_6,_2025_(cropped).jpg","author":"Cabinet Public Relations Office of the Cabinet Secretariat","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"Edgar Lungu in TICAD VII (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Edgar_Lungu_in_TICAD_VII_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Edgar_Lungu_in_TICAD_VII_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edgar_Lungu_in_TICAD_VII_(cropped).jpg","author":"Cabinet Public Relations Office of the Cabinet Secretariat","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"Kenneth David Kaunda.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Kenneth_David_Kaunda.jpg/330px-Kenneth_David_Kaunda.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kenneth_David_Kaunda.jpg","author":"Unknown photographer","license":"Public domain"},"Guy Scott.png":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Guy_Scott.png/330px-Guy_Scott.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guy_Scott.png","author":"Amanda Lucidon / White House","license":"Public domain"},"Levy Mwanawasa.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Levy_Mwanawasa.jpg/330px-Levy_Mwanawasa.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Levy_Mwanawasa.jpg","author":"International Monetary Fund","license":"Public domain"},"Rupiah Banda.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Rupiah_Banda.jpg/330px-Rupiah_Banda.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rupiah_Banda.jpg","author":"Antonio Cruz/ABr","license":"CC BY-SA 2.5"},"Frederick Chiluba on February 3, 1994 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Frederick_Chiluba_on_February_3%2C_1994_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Frederick_Chiluba_on_February_3%2C_1994_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frederick_Chiluba_on_February_3,_1994_(cropped).jpg","author":"European Communities, 1994 / EC - Audiovisual